stateDiagram-v2
    %% CURRENT implementation; sources and guards in transition inventory.
    state "NOTHING id=0 (reference; entry UNKNOWN)" as NOTHING
    state "ACTIVE id=1" as ACTIVE
    state "EXPIRED id=102 (historical)" as EXPIRED
    state "RESTRICTED id=103 (historical)" as RESTRICTED
    state "REVOKED id=104" as REVOKED
    state "rotated_at present (derived; status retained)" as rotated
    [*] --> ACTIVE
    ACTIVE --> REVOKED: revoke!
    ACTIVE --> rotated: refresh rotation replaces the token row
    note right of ACTIVE
        DeviceSession is locked before token rotation or revocation.
        EXPIRED and RESTRICTED are historical labels; no new writer
        restores them or promotes a terminal row.
        RESTRICTED (103) was the retired session-limit placeholder; the
        session-limit waiting unit is a resolution child, never a token row.
    end note
